From: Beryl 7 integration <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7996: bypass broken SDO TX path on MT7990

The connac3 SDO firmware path builds TX descriptors for normal 802.3
unicast data frames. On MT7990 this path can produce malformed TX
descriptor/rate fields and severely reduce AP-to-client throughput.

Force host TXWI/TXD generation for MT7990 only. Keep the SDO path
unchanged for MT7996 and MT7992.

This is the host-fill workaround described in openwrt/mt76 issues #1043
and #1065, adapted to the host_txd boolean used by the pinned mt76
revision. The equivalent upstream behavior was present before SDO was
re-enabled (commit 325a0c49); commit 55218e6 re-enabled SDO.

--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1143,6 +1143,6 @@ int mt7996_tx_prepare_skb(struct mt76_dev *mdev, void *txwi_ptr,
 
 	/* mt76_tx_status_skb_add() clears info->control.flags */
-	host_txd = !is_8023 ||
+	host_txd = !is_8023 || is_mt7990(&dev->mt76) ||
 		   (info->control.flags & (IEEE80211_TX_CTRL_STREAM_CLASSIFIED |
 					   IEEE80211_TX_CTRL_EXPLICIT_UP));
 
